[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186133891 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ca5fbd9d-06c2-5516-a2aa-caaa1b2a1fc6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133892 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2f9d1bf2-2ca6-5610-aed1-5f5054aae288"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133893 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ada3d128-ac86-51c2-88c8-3e672e4cad88"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ca5fbd9d-06c2-5516-a2aa-caaa1b2a1fc6" :question/id #uuid "ca5fbd9d-06c2-5516-a2aa-caaa1b2a1fc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-124246" :question/problem "![](images/88/88da0f1ddf1f605186c9d921a9eade24b5f0aa9de2ae4afdc51a921586093b16.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along the line segment from the point $(-2,3)$ to the point $(0,0),$ as shown above?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=⟨2t-2,\\,3-3t⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a line segment with endpoints $(-2,3)$ and $(0,0).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨(-2+t(0-(-2))),\\,(3+t(0-3))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t-2,\\,3-3t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-2)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={x}^{2}y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(2t-2)^{2}(3-3t) \\\\  & =4(t-1)^{2}\\cdot 3(1-t) \\\\  & =-12(t-1)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}-12(t-1)^{3}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-24{\\int }_{0}^{1}(t-1)^{3}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d86ee8d9-aeae-5ab1-b4a0-98c765570dca"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d86ee8d9-aeae-5ab1-b4a0-98c765570dca" :answer-field/id #uuid "d86ee8d9-aeae-5ab1-b4a0-98c765570dca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5550e6c3-7324-5809-9dfc-0f8be5c60c9e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-78816eec-e214-5a4a-a51d-fa5102203d98" "answer-5550e6c3-7324-5809-9dfc-0f8be5c60c9e" "answer-1b787a8e-ad68-5398-92d2-2ebf1e8be534" "answer-02ba6004-1436-5e5b-ae2f-735e7eb45f4f" "answer-9756d62a-6b6c-5317-a183-008b9c4d2660"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78816eec-e214-5a4a-a51d-fa5102203d98" :answer/id #uuid "78816eec-e214-5a4a-a51d-fa5102203d98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12{\\int }_{0}^{1}(t-1)^{3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5550e6c3-7324-5809-9dfc-0f8be5c60c9e" :answer/id #uuid "5550e6c3-7324-5809-9dfc-0f8be5c60c9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-24{\\int }_{0}^{1}(t-1)^{3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b787a8e-ad68-5398-92d2-2ebf1e8be534" :answer/id #uuid "1b787a8e-ad68-5398-92d2-2ebf1e8be534" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t-1)^{3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02ba6004-1436-5e5b-ae2f-735e7eb45f4f" :answer/id #uuid "02ba6004-1436-5e5b-ae2f-735e7eb45f4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24{\\int }_{0}^{1}(t-3)^{3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9756d62a-6b6c-5317-a183-008b9c4d2660" :answer/id #uuid "9756d62a-6b6c-5317-a183-008b9c4d2660" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t-1)^{3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2f9d1bf2-2ca6-5610-aed1-5f5054aae288" :question/id #uuid "2f9d1bf2-2ca6-5610-aed1-5f5054aae288" :question/math-academy-id "q-124272" :question/problem "![](images/f5/f5f5b235b54d2acd20297ab365d9b93907111b3fec9a86776c28e93fdfe105ee.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along the line segment from the point $(0,0)$ to the point $(2,3),$ as shown above?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=⟨2t,\\,3t⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a line segment with endpoints $(0,0)$ and $(2,3).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨(0+t(2-0)),\\,(0+t(3-0))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,3t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(2t)^{2}+(3t)^{2} \\\\  & =4{t}^{2}+9{t}^{2} \\\\  & =13{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}13{t}^{2}\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =39{\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2c3bc565-6668-5708-9572-740391604ada"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2c3bc565-6668-5708-9572-740391604ada" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c3bc565-6668-5708-9572-740391604ada" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f113768c-cf48-5fce-945b-53b72f33cbc9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8b05db23-972c-567b-8223-11bddcab9b32" "answer-25e50d33-12b9-5c12-ac4e-4e3135ef41df" "answer-a18fa886-a66f-5c1c-a378-38efae13d666" "answer-f113768c-cf48-5fce-945b-53b72f33cbc9" "answer-92ad03ae-93a6-5758-8869-8e58634200a0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b05db23-972c-567b-8223-11bddcab9b32" :answer/id #uuid "8b05db23-972c-567b-8223-11bddcab9b32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13{\\int }_{0}^{1}(3{t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25e50d33-12b9-5c12-ac4e-4e3135ef41df" :answer/id #uuid "25e50d33-12b9-5c12-ac4e-4e3135ef41df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13{\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a18fa886-a66f-5c1c-a378-38efae13d666" :answer/id #uuid "a18fa886-a66f-5c1c-a378-38efae13d666" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "26{\\int }_{0}^{1}(3{t}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f113768c-cf48-5fce-945b-53b72f33cbc9" :answer/id #uuid "f113768c-cf48-5fce-945b-53b72f33cbc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "39{\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92ad03ae-93a6-5758-8869-8e58634200a0" :answer/id #uuid "92ad03ae-93a6-5758-8869-8e58634200a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{\\int }_{0}^{1}(3-{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ada3d128-ac86-51c2-88c8-3e672e4cad88" :question/id #uuid "ada3d128-ac86-51c2-88c8-3e672e4cad88" :question/math-academy-id "q-124172" :question/problem "![](images/09/09a38bb4306728f97b7fecbf9ab1bda7aa957607352c1ab27af09489c271c3ed.png)\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{C}({y}^{2}-2x)\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path traversed along the line segment from the point $(0,1)$ to the point $(2,3),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nThe curve $C$ is a line segment with endpoints $(0,1)$ and $(2,3).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨(0+t(2-0)),\\,(1+t(3-1))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,1+2t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+2t)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={y}^{2}-2x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(1+2t)^{2}-2(2t) \\\\  & =1+4t+4{t}^{2}-4t \\\\  & =4{t}^{2}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4{t}^{2}+1)\\cdot 2\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4{t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{[\\frac{4{t}^{3}}{3}+t]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{4}{3}+1)-2(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8b9c47c5-4e96-58fa-ac91-5791dc11f30c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8b9c47c5-4e96-58fa-ac91-5791dc11f30c" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b9c47c5-4e96-58fa-ac91-5791dc11f30c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6029d8a7-a6ae-5959-9ee4-f8e3ebd8e072" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c94fc212-35ff-5e38-9f57-12d4f4959a4c" "answer-6029d8a7-a6ae-5959-9ee4-f8e3ebd8e072" "answer-21702398-6680-552d-923f-027dff95a35a" "answer-ea8f272e-677d-5489-96d8-1e29db88e990" "answer-78ae96ca-4942-5362-807b-c0b65d2496c2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c94fc212-35ff-5e38-9f57-12d4f4959a4c" :answer/id #uuid "c94fc212-35ff-5e38-9f57-12d4f4959a4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6029d8a7-a6ae-5959-9ee4-f8e3ebd8e072" :answer/id #uuid "6029d8a7-a6ae-5959-9ee4-f8e3ebd8e072" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21702398-6680-552d-923f-027dff95a35a" :answer/id #uuid "21702398-6680-552d-923f-027dff95a35a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea8f272e-677d-5489-96d8-1e29db88e990" :answer/id #uuid "ea8f272e-677d-5489-96d8-1e29db88e990" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78ae96ca-4942-5362-807b-c0b65d2496c2" :answer/id #uuid "78ae96ca-4942-5362-807b-c0b65d2496c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135122 :tutorial/content "Until now, we've been dealing with line integrals with respect to arc length. In this lesson, we will learn about other types of line integral. \n\nSuppose that $C$ is a path in the $xy$-plane with initial point $A$ and terminal point $B.$ The line integral of the function $f(x,y)$ **with respect to $\\boldsymbol x$** along the path $C$ is denoted\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nTo understand what this integral represents, we imagine traversing $C$ from $A$ to $B.$ At each point $P$ that lies on $C,$ we project the point on $f$ that lies directly above $P$ onto the plane $y=0.$ Doing this for every point on $C$ traces out a curve. The line integral of $f$ with respect to $x$ gives the (signed) area bounded by this curve and the $x$-axis.\n\n![](images/62/62c07a36cbf79459021ee7be125536a8f9c1bc3c193a99eabfcd3fc851b8eb0c.png)\n\nTo calculate a line integral with respect to $x,$ we must first parameterize $C$ using a parameter $t\\in [a,b].$ Then, we apply the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}x  = \\int\\limits_a^b  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\dfrac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nLet's take a look at a concrete example." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133995 :activity/expected-seconds 900.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-ca5fbd9d-06c2-5516-a2aa-caaa1b2a1fc6" :question/id #uuid "ca5fbd9d-06c2-5516-a2aa-caaa1b2a1fc6"] ["question-ca5fbd9d-06c2-5516-a2aa-caaa1b2a1fc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-124246"] ["question-ca5fbd9d-06c2-5516-a2aa-caaa1b2a1fc6" :question/problem "![](images/88/88da0f1ddf1f605186c9d921a9eade24b5f0aa9de2ae4afdc51a921586093b16.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along the line segment from the point $(-2,3)$ to the point $(0,0),$ as shown above?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=⟨2t-2,\\,3-3t⟩.$*"] ["question-ca5fbd9d-06c2-5516-a2aa-caaa1b2a1fc6" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a line segment with endpoints $(-2,3)$ and $(0,0).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨(-2+t(0-(-2))),\\,(3+t(0-3))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t-2,\\,3-3t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-2)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={x}^{2}y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(2t-2)^{2}(3-3t) \\\\  & =4(t-1)^{2}\\cdot 3(1-t) \\\\  & =-12(t-1)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}-12(t-1)^{3}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-24{\\int }_{0}^{1}(t-1)^{3}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-ca5fbd9d-06c2-5516-a2aa-caaa1b2a1fc6" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-d86ee8d9-aeae-5ab1-b4a0-98c765570dca" :answer-field/id #uuid "d86ee8d9-aeae-5ab1-b4a0-98c765570dca"] ["answer-78816eec-e214-5a4a-a51d-fa5102203d98" :answer/id #uuid "78816eec-e214-5a4a-a51d-fa5102203d98"] ["answer-78816eec-e214-5a4a-a51d-fa5102203d98" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-78816eec-e214-5a4a-a51d-fa5102203d98" :answer/value "-12{\\int }_{0}^{1}(t-1)^{3}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["answer-5550e6c3-7324-5809-9dfc-0f8be5c60c9e" :answer/id #uuid "5550e6c3-7324-5809-9dfc-0f8be5c60c9e"] ["answer-5550e6c3-7324-5809-9dfc-0f8be5c60c9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5550e6c3-7324-5809-9dfc-0f8be5c60c9e" :answer/value "-24{\\int }_{0}^{1}(t-1)^{3}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["answer-1b787a8e-ad68-5398-92d2-2ebf1e8be534" :answer/id #uuid "1b787a8e-ad68-5398-92d2-2ebf1e8be534"] ["answer-1b787a8e-ad68-5398-92d2-2ebf1e8be534" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1b787a8e-ad68-5398-92d2-2ebf1e8be534" :answer/value "-3{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t-1)^{3}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["answer-02ba6004-1436-5e5b-ae2f-735e7eb45f4f" :answer/id #uuid "02ba6004-1436-5e5b-ae2f-735e7eb45f4f"] ["answer-02ba6004-1436-5e5b-ae2f-735e7eb45f4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-02ba6004-1436-5e5b-ae2f-735e7eb45f4f" :answer/value "24{\\int }_{0}^{1}(t-3)^{3}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["answer-9756d62a-6b6c-5317-a183-008b9c4d2660" :answer/id #uuid "9756d62a-6b6c-5317-a183-008b9c4d2660"] ["answer-9756d62a-6b6c-5317-a183-008b9c4d2660" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9756d62a-6b6c-5317-a183-008b9c4d2660" :answer/value "6{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t-1)^{3}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["answer-field-d86ee8d9-aeae-5ab1-b4a0-98c765570dca" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-d86ee8d9-aeae-5ab1-b4a0-98c765570dca" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-d86ee8d9-aeae-5ab1-b4a0-98c765570dca" :answer-field/correct "answer-5550e6c3-7324-5809-9dfc-0f8be5c60c9e"] ["answer-field-d86ee8d9-aeae-5ab1-b4a0-98c765570dca" :answer-field/choices "answer-78816eec-e214-5a4a-a51d-fa5102203d98"] ["answer-field-d86ee8d9-aeae-5ab1-b4a0-98c765570dca" :answer-field/choices "answer-5550e6c3-7324-5809-9dfc-0f8be5c60c9e"] ["answer-field-d86ee8d9-aeae-5ab1-b4a0-98c765570dca" :answer-field/choices "answer-1b787a8e-ad68-5398-92d2-2ebf1e8be534"] ["answer-field-d86ee8d9-aeae-5ab1-b4a0-98c765570dca" :answer-field/choices "answer-02ba6004-1436-5e5b-ae2f-735e7eb45f4f"] ["answer-field-d86ee8d9-aeae-5ab1-b4a0-98c765570dca" :answer-field/choices "answer-9756d62a-6b6c-5317-a183-008b9c4d2660"] ["question-ca5fbd9d-06c2-5516-a2aa-caaa1b2a1fc6" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-d86ee8d9-aeae-5ab1-b4a0-98c765570dca"] [17592186133891 :knowledge-point/questions "question-ca5fbd9d-06c2-5516-a2aa-caaa1b2a1fc6"] ["question-2f9d1bf2-2ca6-5610-aed1-5f5054aae288" :question/id #uuid "2f9d1bf2-2ca6-5610-aed1-5f5054aae288"] ["question-2f9d1bf2-2ca6-5610-aed1-5f5054aae288" :question/math-academy-id "q-124272"] ["question-2f9d1bf2-2ca6-5610-aed1-5f5054aae288" :question/problem "![](images/f5/f5f5b235b54d2acd20297ab365d9b93907111b3fec9a86776c28e93fdfe105ee.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along the line segment from the point $(0,0)$ to the point $(2,3),$ as shown above?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=⟨2t,\\,3t⟩.$*"] ["question-2f9d1bf2-2ca6-5610-aed1-5f5054aae288" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a line segment with endpoints $(0,0)$ and $(2,3).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨(0+t(2-0)),\\,(0+t(3-0))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,3t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(2t)^{2}+(3t)^{2} \\\\  & =4{t}^{2}+9{t}^{2} \\\\  & =13{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}13{t}^{2}\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =39{\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-2f9d1bf2-2ca6-5610-aed1-5f5054aae288" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-2c3bc565-6668-5708-9572-740391604ada" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c3bc565-6668-5708-9572-740391604ada"] ["answer-8b05db23-972c-567b-8223-11bddcab9b32" :answer/id #uuid "8b05db23-972c-567b-8223-11bddcab9b32"] ["answer-8b05db23-972c-567b-8223-11bddcab9b32" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8b05db23-972c-567b-8223-11bddcab9b32" :answer/value "13{\\int }_{0}^{1}(3{t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t"] ["answer-25e50d33-12b9-5c12-ac4e-4e3135ef41df" :answer/id #uuid "25e50d33-12b9-5c12-ac4e-4e3135ef41df"] ["answer-25e50d33-12b9-5c12-ac4e-4e3135ef41df" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-25e50d33-12b9-5c12-ac4e-4e3135ef41df" :answer/value "13{\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["answer-a18fa886-a66f-5c1c-a378-38efae13d666" :answer/id #uuid "a18fa886-a66f-5c1c-a378-38efae13d666"] ["answer-a18fa886-a66f-5c1c-a378-38efae13d666" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a18fa886-a66f-5c1c-a378-38efae13d666" :answer/value "26{\\int }_{0}^{1}(3{t}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}t"] ["answer-f113768c-cf48-5fce-945b-53b72f33cbc9" :answer/id #uuid "f113768c-cf48-5fce-945b-53b72f33cbc9"] ["answer-f113768c-cf48-5fce-945b-53b72f33cbc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f113768c-cf48-5fce-945b-53b72f33cbc9" :answer/value "39{\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["answer-92ad03ae-93a6-5758-8869-8e58634200a0" :answer/id #uuid "92ad03ae-93a6-5758-8869-8e58634200a0"] ["answer-92ad03ae-93a6-5758-8869-8e58634200a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-92ad03ae-93a6-5758-8869-8e58634200a0" :answer/value "9{\\int }_{0}^{1}(3-{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t"] ["answer-field-2c3bc565-6668-5708-9572-740391604ada" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-2c3bc565-6668-5708-9572-740391604ada" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-2c3bc565-6668-5708-9572-740391604ada" :answer-field/correct "answer-f113768c-cf48-5fce-945b-53b72f33cbc9"] ["answer-field-2c3bc565-6668-5708-9572-740391604ada" :answer-field/choices "answer-8b05db23-972c-567b-8223-11bddcab9b32"] ["answer-field-2c3bc565-6668-5708-9572-740391604ada" :answer-field/choices "answer-25e50d33-12b9-5c12-ac4e-4e3135ef41df"] ["answer-field-2c3bc565-6668-5708-9572-740391604ada" :answer-field/choices "answer-a18fa886-a66f-5c1c-a378-38efae13d666"] ["answer-field-2c3bc565-6668-5708-9572-740391604ada" :answer-field/choices "answer-f113768c-cf48-5fce-945b-53b72f33cbc9"] ["answer-field-2c3bc565-6668-5708-9572-740391604ada" :answer-field/choices "answer-92ad03ae-93a6-5758-8869-8e58634200a0"] ["question-2f9d1bf2-2ca6-5610-aed1-5f5054aae288" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-2c3bc565-6668-5708-9572-740391604ada"] [17592186133892 :knowledge-point/questions "question-2f9d1bf2-2ca6-5610-aed1-5f5054aae288"] ["question-ada3d128-ac86-51c2-88c8-3e672e4cad88" :question/id #uuid "ada3d128-ac86-51c2-88c8-3e672e4cad88"] ["question-ada3d128-ac86-51c2-88c8-3e672e4cad88" :question/math-academy-id "q-124172"] ["question-ada3d128-ac86-51c2-88c8-3e672e4cad88" :question/problem "![](images/09/09a38bb4306728f97b7fecbf9ab1bda7aa957607352c1ab27af09489c271c3ed.png)\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{C}({y}^{2}-2x)\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path traversed along the line segment from the point $(0,1)$ to the point $(2,3),$ as shown above."] ["question-ada3d128-ac86-51c2-88c8-3e672e4cad88" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nThe curve $C$ is a line segment with endpoints $(0,1)$ and $(2,3).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨(0+t(2-0)),\\,(1+t(3-1))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,1+2t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+2t)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={y}^{2}-2x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(1+2t)^{2}-2(2t) \\\\  & =1+4t+4{t}^{2}-4t \\\\  & =4{t}^{2}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4{t}^{2}+1)\\cdot 2\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4{t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{[\\frac{4{t}^{3}}{3}+t]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{4}{3}+1)-2(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-ada3d128-ac86-51c2-88c8-3e672e4cad88" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-8b9c47c5-4e96-58fa-ac91-5791dc11f30c" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b9c47c5-4e96-58fa-ac91-5791dc11f30c"] ["answer-c94fc212-35ff-5e38-9f57-12d4f4959a4c" :answer/id #uuid "c94fc212-35ff-5e38-9f57-12d4f4959a4c"] ["answer-c94fc212-35ff-5e38-9f57-12d4f4959a4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c94fc212-35ff-5e38-9f57-12d4f4959a4c" :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}"] ["answer-6029d8a7-a6ae-5959-9ee4-f8e3ebd8e072" :answer/id #uuid "6029d8a7-a6ae-5959-9ee4-f8e3ebd8e072"] ["answer-6029d8a7-a6ae-5959-9ee4-f8e3ebd8e072" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6029d8a7-a6ae-5959-9ee4-f8e3ebd8e072" :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}"] ["answer-21702398-6680-552d-923f-027dff95a35a" :answer/id #uuid "21702398-6680-552d-923f-027dff95a35a"] ["answer-21702398-6680-552d-923f-027dff95a35a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-21702398-6680-552d-923f-027dff95a35a" :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["answer-ea8f272e-677d-5489-96d8-1e29db88e990" :answer/id #uuid "ea8f272e-677d-5489-96d8-1e29db88e990"] ["answer-ea8f272e-677d-5489-96d8-1e29db88e990" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ea8f272e-677d-5489-96d8-1e29db88e990" :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}"] ["answer-78ae96ca-4942-5362-807b-c0b65d2496c2" :answer/id #uuid "78ae96ca-4942-5362-807b-c0b65d2496c2"] ["answer-78ae96ca-4942-5362-807b-c0b65d2496c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-78ae96ca-4942-5362-807b-c0b65d2496c2" :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}"] ["answer-field-8b9c47c5-4e96-58fa-ac91-5791dc11f30c" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-8b9c47c5-4e96-58fa-ac91-5791dc11f30c" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-8b9c47c5-4e96-58fa-ac91-5791dc11f30c" :answer-field/correct "answer-6029d8a7-a6ae-5959-9ee4-f8e3ebd8e072"] ["answer-field-8b9c47c5-4e96-58fa-ac91-5791dc11f30c" :answer-field/choices "answer-c94fc212-35ff-5e38-9f57-12d4f4959a4c"] ["answer-field-8b9c47c5-4e96-58fa-ac91-5791dc11f30c" :answer-field/choices "answer-6029d8a7-a6ae-5959-9ee4-f8e3ebd8e072"] ["answer-field-8b9c47c5-4e96-58fa-ac91-5791dc11f30c" :answer-field/choices "answer-21702398-6680-552d-923f-027dff95a35a"] ["answer-field-8b9c47c5-4e96-58fa-ac91-5791dc11f30c" :answer-field/choices "answer-ea8f272e-677d-5489-96d8-1e29db88e990"] ["answer-field-8b9c47c5-4e96-58fa-ac91-5791dc11f30c" :answer-field/choices "answer-78ae96ca-4942-5362-807b-c0b65d2496c2"] ["question-ada3d128-ac86-51c2-88c8-3e672e4cad88" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-8b9c47c5-4e96-58fa-ac91-5791dc11f30c"] [17592186133893 :knowledge-point/questions "question-ada3d128-ac86-51c2-88c8-3e672e4cad88"] [17592186135122 :tutorial/content "Until now, we've been dealing with line integrals with respect to arc length. In this lesson, we will learn about other types of line integral. \n\nSuppose that $C$ is a path in the $xy$-plane with initial point $A$ and terminal point $B.$ The line integral of the function $f(x,y)$ **with respect to $\\boldsymbol x$** along the path $C$ is denoted\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nTo understand what this integral represents, we imagine traversing $C$ from $A$ to $B.$ At each point $P$ that lies on $C,$ we project the point on $f$ that lies directly above $P$ onto the plane $y=0.$ Doing this for every point on $C$ traces out a curve. The line integral of $f$ with respect to $x$ gives the (signed) area bounded by this curve and the $x$-axis.\n\n![](images/62/62c07a36cbf79459021ee7be125536a8f9c1bc3c193a99eabfcd3fc851b8eb0c.png)\n\nTo calculate a line integral with respect to $x,$ we must first parameterize $C$ using a parameter $t\\in [a,b].$ Then, we apply the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}x  = \\int\\limits_a^b  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\dfrac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nLet's take a look at a concrete example."] [17592186133995 :activity/expected-seconds 900.0]] "retractions" [[17592186135122 :tutorial/content "Until now, we've been dealing with line integrals with respect to arc length. In this lesson, we will learn about other types of line integral. \n\nSuppose that $C$ is a path in the $xy$-plane with initial point $A$ and terminal point $B.$ The line integral of the function $f(x,y)$ **with respect to $\\boldsymbol x$** along the path $C$ is denoted\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nTo understand what this integral represents, we imagine traversing $C$ from $A$ to $B.$ At each point $P$ that lies on $C,$ we project the point on $f$ that lies directly above $P$ onto the plane $y=0.$ Doing this for every point on $C$ traces out a curve. The line integral of $f$ with respect to $x$ gives the (signed) area bounded by this curve and the $x$-axis.\n\nThis integral represents the total area accumulated when [math]f[/math] is projected on the plane [math]y=0[/math] as [math]C[/math] is traversed from the initial point [math]A[/math] to the terminal point [math]B.[/math] \n\n![](images/62/62c07a36cbf79459021ee7be125536a8f9c1bc3c193a99eabfcd3fc851b8eb0c.png)\n\nTo calculate a line integral with respect to $x,$ we must first parameterize $C$ using a parameter $t\\in [a,b].$ Then, we apply the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}x  = \\int\\limits_a^b  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\dfrac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nLet's take a look at a concrete example."]]}]